lifeos-nix patch f2 — Skip runtime `bun install` in DeployCore (deps are Nix-vendored)

PROBLEM
  DeployCore.ts runs `bun install` at activation time, reaching the npm registry from a
  user machine at first launch (RedTeam CR-3). 7.40.4 does this in TWO places:
    (d) deployDependencies      — one `bun install` in configRoot (the original CR-3 spot)
    (e) deployNestedDependencies — NEW (PR #1581/#1605/#1739): walks the runtime tree +
        every shipped skill dir and runs `bun install --cwd` per package.json, plus a
        Next.js build of the Observability dashboard. Unpatched, this re-opens the exact
        egress hole f2 closed, and breaks offline/hermetic activation.

ROOT CAUSE
  Upstream's AI-native install assumes deps are fetched at activation; Nix packaging
  requires all deps resolved at build time (fixed-output derivations, offline).

SCOPE
  Touches only DeployCore.ts, neutralizing BOTH install paths (d + e). node_modules are
  vendored into the store by the derivation and bridged into configRoot by the `lifeos`
  launcher (the 5 core trees + the in-place skill trees Evals/Prompting). Un-bridged skill
  trees are either external-service-dead (deliberately unvendored) or runtime-instantiated
  templates. The Observability dashboard ships pre-built (out/index.html) from the
  derivation, so step (e)'s rebuild is dead weight too.

VERIFICATION
  ISC-133 egress test: full DeployCore activation chain in a deny-all rootless netns with
  strace — zero external connect() attempts, activation exit 0. Build green.

RE-PORTED to upstream v7.40.4 (be9e8ef): step (e) is new since 7.1.1; regenerated against
7.40.4 source to cover both install paths.

